    },
    {
      "nivel": 2,
      "titulo": "What the service checks on a 911 Turbo",
      "parrafos": [],
      "items": [
        "Turbo, wastegate and blow-off valves: boost pressure, shaft play and oil leaks. On the 930, also the intercooler and its hoses.",
        "Oil and filter with oil suited to turbo temperatures, and cooling: radiators, pump and thermostat, which work harder on a Turbo.",
        "Clutch and gearbox, manual or PDK, and four-wheel drive from the 993: transfer case, propshaft and front differential.",
        "Brakes: Turbos carry the biggest brakes of their generation and wear them at their own pace. Brake fluid included.",
        "Alignment and tyres: wide sizes and fast rear wear, and on the 930, a check that the geometry has not moved."
      ],
